#############################################################################################################
                                       UniDesign (Version 20230524)
  A command-line-based tool featuring protein structure modeling and protein design, including:

    *) de novo protein sequence design and protein sequence redesign (ProteinDesign)
       can be used to design monomer proteins, protein-protein interactions, protein-ligand interactions, 
       protein-nucleic acid interactions, and enzymes
    *) protein side-chain packing (ProteinDesign in conjuncion with the option --wildtype_only)
    *) calculate protein fold stability score (ComputeStability)
    *) calculate protein-protein binding energy score (ComputeBinding)
    *) repair missing protein side chains (RepairStructure)
    *) protein structure energy minimization (Minimize)
    *) build mutant strucure models (BuildMutant)
    *) add polar hydrogen atoms (AddPolarHydrogen)
    *) optimize hydrogen's position to maximize hydrogen bonding networks (OptimizeHydrogen)

  Copyright (c) Xiaoqiang Huang
  Contact: xiaoqiah@outlook.com
############################################################################################################

command 'ProteinDesign' is supported
unknown option -- lig_atomparam
Usage: UniDesign [OPTIONS]

OPTIONS:
   -v              print version
   --version       print version
   -h              print help message
   -?              print help message
   --help          print help message
   --command=arg   choose your command:
                   [Energy calculation module]
                     ComputeStability
                     ComputeBinding
                     ComputeEvolutionScore
                     ComputeResiEnergy
                     ComputeRotamersEnergy
                   [Structure modeling module]
                     RepairStructure
                     Minimize
                     BuildMutant
                     AddPolarHydrogen
                     OptimizeHydrogen
                     ProteinDesign
                   [ProteinDesign and side-chain packing module]
                     monomer design: ProteinDesign --monomer
                     PPI design    : ProteinDesign --ppint
                     PLI design    : ProteinDesign --protlig
                     enzyme design : ProteinDesign --enzyme
                     packing       : ProteinDesign --wildtype_only
                   [Enzyme and PLI design module]
                     MakeLigParamAndTopo
                     MakeLigPoses
                     AnalyzeLigPoses
                     ScreenLigPoses
                   [Structure checking and assessment module]
                     CheckClash0
                     CheckClash1
                     CheckClash2
                     CheckResiInRotLib
                     CompareSideChain
                     FindCoreResidue
                     FindInterfaceResidue
                     FindIntermediateResidue
                     FindSurfaceResidue
                     GetPhiPsi
                     GetResiMinRMSD
                     GetResiBfactor
                     ShowResiComposition
                   [Sequence-based feature prediction module]
                     PhiPsiPred
                     SSPred
                     SAPred
                   [Other modules]
                     OptimizeWeight

command can be used in conjunction with one or more following options:

   --pdb=arg                 arg is a standard readable PDB file
   --split_chains=arg        arg specifies chain splitting for ComputeBinding with >=3 protein chains (e.g. AB,C or AB,CDE)
   --mutant_file=arg         arg is a file recording one or more mutants
   --bbdep=arg               arg = yes/no, turning on/off the flag for using bb-dep rotamer library (default: yes)
   --use_input_sc            use input protein structure's side chains as rotamers
   --ppi_shell1=arg          arg is the distance cutoff for the 1st shell of PPI (default: 5.0 Angstroms)
   --ppi_shell2=arg          arg is the distance cutoff for the 2nd shell of PPI (default: 8.0 Angstroms)
   --evolution               protein design using both physics and evolution scores
   --physics                 protein design using physical scoring function (EvoEF) only (default)
   --monomer                 the designing protein is treated as a monomer
   --ppint                   protein-protein interaction design
   --protlig                 protein-ligand interaction design
   --enzyme                  enzyme design (extended version of PLI design) with catalytic constraints
   --design_chains=arg       arg is the designing chain(s)'s identifier (e.g. A, or AB)
   --mol2=arg                arg is a standard readable mol2 file, atomic charge should be included
   --rotate_hydroxyl=arg     arg = yes/no, turning on/off the flag for rotating Ser, Thr, and Tyr hydroxyl hydrogen (default: on)
   --xdeviation=arg          arg is a float value cutoff for side-chain Chi angle deviation
   --wread=arg               arg is a energy-weight file
   --pdblist=arg             arg is a file recording a list of PDB IDs, each in one line
   --wildtype_only
   --rotlib=arg              arg is the name of a rotamer lib
   --pdb2=arg                arg is the 2nd PDB file for comparing side-chains by command CompareSideChain
                             this flag makes design very slow (default: turned off)
   --pli_shell1=arg          arg is the distance cutoff for the 1st shell of protein-ligand interaction (default: 5.0 Angstroms)
   --pli_shell2=arg          arg is the distance cutoff for the 2nd shell of protein-ligand interaction (default: 8.0 Angstroms)
   --clash_ratio=arg         arg is a float value cutoff for the command CheckClash[0-2] (default: 0.6)
   --ntraj=arg               arg is an integer for the number of independent protein design trajectories (default: 1)
   --excl_low_prob=arg       arg is a flat value cutoff for excluding low-probability rotamers (default: 0.03), 0~0.05 suggested
   --interface_only
   --seq=arg                 arg is a single-line plain-text FASTA protein sequence file
   --evo_allterms            turn on the flag for using all-term evolution (including PSSM, SA, SS, and psi-phi) for protein design
   --wprof=arg               arg is a float value (default: 1.0)
   --resfile=arg             arg is the name of residue-restriction file
   --seed_from_nat           turn on the flag for using native sequence as a starting point for protein design
   --excl_rot_cys            exclude the Cystenine rotamers for protein design
   --show_hydrogen=arg       arg = yes, save the coordinates of polar hydrogens to PDB file
                             arg = no, do not write hydrogens into PDB
   --ncut_cb_core=arg        arg is an integer cutoff value for the number of CB atoms for a CORE (buried) residue (default: 20)
   --ncut_cb_surf=arg        arg is an integer cutoff value for the number of CB atoms for a SURFACE (exposed) residue (default: 15)
   --init_3atoms=arg         arg is the name of three atoms divided by commas (e.g. C1,C2,C3)
                             this option is only used with the command GenLigParamAndTopo
   --read_lig_poses=arg      read ligand poses from the file arg, a PDB file recording multiple ligand poses
   --write_lig_poses=arg     write ligand poses to the file arg, a PDB file for recording multiple ligand poses
   --scrn_by_orientation=arg        screen ligand poses using the rule defined in the arg file
   --scrn_by_vdw=arg      screen ligand poses with both internalVDW and backboneVDW ranked in a low percentile, e.g. 25%
   --scrn_by_rmsd=arg        screen ligand poses using an RMSD cutoff value (default: 1.0)


